EXT. SHELLED FARMHOUSE COURTYARD, NORMANDY - DAWN

Mist. Broken tile. A dead cow on its side, bloated.

Three soldiers crouch behind a collapsed wall.

SERGEANT EZEKIEL "ZEKE" MATTHIAS-ODUYA (30s, helmet netted, chewing nothing) peers over the stones.

Beside him, PRIVATE COLM BRANNIGAN-VOSS (19, rifle too big, freckles) breathes through his mouth.

Behind them, CORPORAL RAFAELA "RAFA" DELGADO-HOLM (20s, radio on her back, steady hands) checks her sidearm.

ZEKE
Quiet. Too quiet.

COLM
You say that every time, Sarge.

ZEKE
It's true every time.

RAFA
Barn's clear. House is clear. Nothing on the ridge.

ZEKE
Then why's the cow dead?

RAFA
Shell.

ZEKE
Which shell?

COLM
Ours?

ZEKE
Maybe.

A bird lands on the cow. Pecks. Leaves.

COLM
Corporal Delgado-Holm. Can I ask something?

RAFA
Rafa. Just Rafa.

COLM
Rafa. Why's the radio quiet?

RAFA
Because nobody's talking.

COLM
That's what I mean.

ZEKE
Brannigan. Eyes front.

COLM
Yes, Sarge.

They wait. A droplet of mist rolls from Zeke's helmet and hits the mud.

RAFA
Sarge. Door.

The farmhouse door, which was shut, is now ajar. A hand-width.

ZEKE
(whispering)
Colm. Left. Rafa. Right. On three.

COLM
One.

RAFA
Two.

They rise together, rifles up.

The door swings wide. Out steps a goat. Then a second goat. A third.

The squad stares. The goats stare back.

COLM
Sarge. Was that the thing?

ZEKE
(deadpan)
That was the thing.

RAFA
I'm going to be sick.

She laughs, covering her mouth. Colm sinks down, giggling. Zeke slumps against the wall, shoulders shaking.

A whistle in the sky. Rising.

They all stop laughing at once.

ZEKE
Down!

They scatter. The first shell lands in the barn. The wall behind them heaves. The goats bolt in three directions. Dust and straw rain over three helmets.

Rafa pulls Colm flat. Zeke crawls over both of them.

ZEKE (CONT'D)
(shouting)
Rafa! Radio!

RAFA
It's dead!

ZEKE
Then pray!

COLM
To who?

ZEKE
The goats!
